fn floor_cost_debt_roster() -> List<String> {
  list_flat_map(xs: floor_cost_debt_chunks(), f: fn(chunk) { chunk })
}

// THE MEMBERSHIP TEST. A `Bool` over a roster is the right shape here and not the mechanical
// one DESIGN warns about: the question this answers has exactly two states -- withheld or not --
// and the typed disposition that carries WHY lives in `v2.workflow.required_floor`, which is
// where a consumer that needs the reason reads it.
fn floor_cost_debt_holds(name: String) -> Bool {
  any(xs: floor_cost_debt_roster(), predicate: fn(row) { row == name })
}

// ── THE DECLARED RUNG DROP (DESIGN §4b(3)) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// WHAT IS LOST, STATED AT THE HONEST GRAIN: 320 witnesses that PASSED on main run 33109071348
// stop executing. Not "run less often" and not "run elsewhere" -- they run nowhere, and every
// property each one asserted is unguarded from the moment this lands. That is 54.7% of the
// fold's measured CPU and 2.7% of its rows, and the asymmetry is the point: the debt is
// concentrated, so the contract can be carried down by fixing a small number of witnesses.
//
// PREVIOUS RUNG: mechanically preventable -- each of these rows was an executing check that
// would go red if the property it asserts broke.
//
// TEMPORARY RUNG: outside the ladder, not mitigatable. Nothing weaker substitutes: there is no
// cadence, no sampling, no review step that re-asks these questions. A withheld row is simply
// not asked. Calling this "mitigatable" because the source still exists would be exactly the
// rung inflation §4b(1) names, and it is the specific lie that made relocation attractive.
//
// WHY IT IS DECLARED RATHER THAN A DEFECT, and this is the operator's call and not the
// author's: the alternative to withholding is a red required check on every PR for a cost debt
// nobody's diff caused. The ruling of 2026-08-27 is that these rows are broken and do not get
// an exemption that lets them keep spending the budget they broke.
//
// REASON `DeletedWithoutReplacement` rather than `ReplacementStaged`: no replacement is staged.
// Nothing observes these properties while they sit here, and claiming a staged replacement
// would manufacture a comfort the population does not have.
data floor_cost_debt_rung_drop: GuaranteeRungDrop = GuaranteeRungDrop {
  subject: "the 320 witnesses withheld from execution by v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt",
  previous: MechanicallyPreventable,
  temporary: OutsideTheLadder,
  reason: DeletedWithoutReplacement {},
  population: [
    "v2.workflow.floor_cost_debt floor_cost_debt_roster"
  ],
  restoration_trigger: "THE ROSTER REACHING EMPTY, AND NOTHING ELSE. Each identity retires by being made to pass under required_floor_claim_cpu_safety_limit_ms and having its line deleted; the row retires when the last line goes. The trigger is deliberately NOT 'a long lane exists that executes them' and NOT 'the ceiling is re-examined': both would satisfy this row while leaving the properties unobserved, which is the trigger-names-less-than-the-capability defect DESIGN §4b(3) records against itself. The capability lost is EXECUTION OF THESE ASSERTIONS, so only their execution restores it."
}
